WUQ7"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables RNA binding activity. Involved in several processes, including cellular response to cytokine stimulus; negative regulation of cytokine production; and negative regulation of signal transduction. Located in cytosol and nuclear speck. Part of catalytic step 2 spliceosome. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8WUQ7","text":"Plays a role in pre-mRNA splicing by facilitating excision of a subset of introns (PubMed:28062851). Required for the splicing of CDCA5/Sororin, a regulator of sister chromatid cohesion (PubMed:28062851). Involved in the regulation of innate immune response (PubMed:20829348). Acts as a negative regulator of Toll-like receptor, interferon-regulatory factor (IRF) and canonical NF-kappa-B signaling pathways (PubMed:20829348, PubMed:26363554). Contributes to the regulation of transcriptional activation of NF-kappa-B target genes in response to endogenous pro-inflammatory stimuli (PubMed:20829348, PubMed:26363554)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}